    {
      "title": "FSSAI initiates legal action against Nestle India over infant products",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/fssai-initiates-legal-action-against-nestle-india-over-infant-products-126091800519_1.html",
      "description": "The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) on Friday said it has initiated legal action against Nestle India Ltd for alleged non-compliance with food safety norms in three infant nutrition products.\nAccording to FSSAI, it examined NAN Excella Pro Stage 1, Lactogen Pro 1, and a follow-up formula along with their promotional material available on e-commerce platforms.\nIn NAN Excella Pro Stage 1, the regulator flagged claims relating to \"5HMOs\" and \"Whey Protein,\" while in Lactogen Pro 1, it observed a claim describing \"Whey Protein\" as easy to digest, the regulator said in a social media post.\nFSSAI said it had sought clarifications from Nestle India on these claims.\nBoth the products were found to be in contravention of Regulation 4(2) of the Food Safety and Standards (Foods for Infant Nutrition) Regulations, 2020, which restrict promotional claims or material aimed at increasing the saleability of infant foods, as well as Section 3 of the Infant Milk Substitutes, Feed",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-18T08:24:00"
    }
